            "result_text": "Done! I've created `/app/run.py` with the `run_tasks` function that:\n\n**Key features:**\n- Uses `asyncio.Semaphore` to enforce the `max_concurrent` limit\n- Each task runs within the semaphore context, ensuring only the specified number run at once\n- Uses `asyncio.gather(..., return_exceptions=True)` so one task failing doesn't crash others\n- **Cleanup handling**: When KeyboardInterrupt happens, running tasks receive `CancelledError`, which allows their `try/finally` blocks to execute cleanup code before the program exits\n\n**How it works:**\n- Tasks are passed as callables (functions that return awaitables) not coroutines\n- The semaphore naturally serializes access while respecting the concurrency limit\n- With `return_exceptions=True`, tasks run independently and exceptions don't cascade\n\nThe tests verify all three scenarios: basic execution, concurrent limit enforcement, and cleanup on cancellation."
